## Architecture rules

- **Request path:** browser → (Vite in dev) → **edge** → the service that owns the URL prefix (`services.json`, longest prefix wins). Services never call the browser-facing edge; they call each other with `ctx.call("<name>", request)`, which stays in the process when both run in `app-all` and goes over HTTP otherwise. Never `reqwest` + `service_url` for another service.
- **Bridges** (`docs/bridges.md`): a service is a library whose `build(ctx)` returns its router and starts its background work (`tokio::spawn`); `main.rs` stays one call. Services never import each other (only `app/` links them), share nothing in memory (the database or `ctx.call`), get only headers from a request (no `ConnectInfo` or other extensions), never open their own database, and run CPU work on `spawn_blocking`.
- **Layers of a service:** `routes.rs` (extract the caller, parse, call logic, map to JSON) → logic/validation module (`model.rs`) → `store.rs` (SQL only) → SQLite. No SQL in handlers, no HTTP types in the store.
- **Ownership:** only the owner service writes a table (named in a `-- [owner]` comment in its migration). Others may read it.
- **Errors:** handlers return `ApiResult<Json<T>>`; errors are `ApiError` (`bad_request`, `unauthorized`, `forbidden`, `not_found`, `conflict`, `unavailable`, `internal`) and reach the client as `{"error": {"code", "message"}}`. Database errors convert automatically.
- **Users:** per-user data is scoped by `app_core::Caller` (`caller.user_id`) in every query.{% if features.auth %} Use `AuthUser` when the handler needs the user's details and `AdminUser` for admin-only routes.{% else %} There is no sign-in yet: every request is the local user `local`; adding accounts only changes `crates/core/src/caller.rs`.{% endif %}
- **Responses:** camelCase JSON (`#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]`), times as Unix ms (`app_core::now_ms()`), ids from `app_core::new_id()` (UUID v7), lists as `{"items": [...]}`.
- **Web:** page → feature store (Pinia) → feature `api.ts` → `@/shared/api/http.ts` (the only `fetch`). A feature imports only `@/shared/**` and its own files.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Builds the workspace, runs the services (as `BRIDGES` says) and Vite on http://localhost:{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}; rebuilds/restarts services on Rust, migration, `services.json` or `.env` changes. `-- --only notes,edge` (separate processes), `-- --no-web` |
| `npm run build` | Type-checks, builds `web/dist` and release binaries (`app-all` and every service) |
| `npm start` | Runs the release builds (by default turns into `app-all`); the edge serves the app and the API on http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}. `node scripts/start.ts` keeps npm out of memory; `-- --check` prints the plan |
| `npm test` | Vitest (web and scripts) + `cargo test --workspace` |
| `npm run check` | The quality gate: ESLint + clippy, Prettier + rustfmt, vue-tsc, all tests |
| `npm run lint` / `npm run format` | Lint only / format everything (Prettier + `cargo fmt`) |
| `cargo test -p app-<name>` | Tests of one crate or service; `cargo test -p app-all`: the whole app in all three modes |
| `npm run setup` | Creates `.env` from `.env.example` with a fresh `MASTER_KEY` (`-- --port-base 9000` shifts every port) |
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}
| `docker compose up --build` | Builds and runs the production container on http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }} |
